{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553415-w20-new-st-help-with-rage-gain-and-moon-phases","id":1553415,"title":"[W20] new ST, help with Rage gain and Moon phases","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-23T16:58:03-07:00","id":1553415,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [W20] new ST, help with Rage gain and Moon phases","content":"Dear community, I'm a new werewolf ST and I'm trying to understand how Rage can be gained seeing the Moon the first time during the night. I'm not a native English speaker so maybe that's why I'm having a bit of confusion.<br /> <br /> From W20 (pag 145) I read:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><b>The Moon:</b></b> The first time a werewolf sees the moon at night, the Beast inside stirs, and Rage floods back into her.<br /> - Under a <b><b>new moon</b></b>, the character gets one point;<br /> - under a <b><b>waning moon</b></b>, two points;<br /> - under a <b><b>half</b></b> or <b><b>waxing moon</b></b>, three points;<br /> - and under a <b><b>full moon</b></b>, four points.<br /> If the moon phase corresponds with the character\u2019s auspice, she regains all of her Rage. This phenomenon only occurs when the character first sees the moon each night. </div> </div> </div>So my understanding is: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_relative text_table_table-fixed\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>Moon Phase</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>Rage gain (CANON)</b></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf11 <b><b>New</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf12 <b><b>Waxing</b></b> Crescent</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3 (?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf13 First Quarter / <b><b>Half</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf14 <b><b>Waxing</b></b> Gibbous</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf15 <b><b>Full</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf16 <b><b>Waning</b></b> Gibbous</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+2 (?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf17 Last Quarter / <b><b>Half</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3 (?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf18 <b><b>Waning</b></b> Crescent</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf11 <b><b>New</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> </tr> </table></div> And it bothers me a bit because of<br /> <br /> <br /> - the +2 jump between &quot;New&quot; and &quot;Waxing Crescent&quot;<br /> - the -2 jump between &quot;Full&quot; and &quot;Waning Gibbous&quot;<br /> - the &quot;Last Quarter&quot; strange rise after the &quot;Waning Gibbous&quot; decrease<br /> <br /> I thought about an errata between editions but also the 1st ed, 2nd ed and Revised core will have the same wording:<br /> <br /> <b><b>1st edition</b></b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><b>The Moon:</b></b> [...] The player gains one point if it is a new moon, two points if it is a waning moon, three points if it is a half or waxing moon, and four points if the moon is full. [...] </div> </div> </div><b><b>2nd edition</b></b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><b>The Moon:</b></b> [...] The character gains one Rage point under a new moon, two points under a waning moon, three points under a half or waxing moon, and four points if the moon is full. [...] </div> </div> </div><b><b>Revised</b></b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><b>The Moon:</b></b> [...] Under a new moon, the character gets one point; under a waning moon, two points; under a half or waxing moon, three points; and under a full moon, four points. [...] </div> </div> </div>So all the core books report this strange &quot;rage gain pattern&quot; (1/3/3/3/4/2/3/2/1).<br /> <br /> So, can you help me finding the reason behind that? Maybe I'm a bit lost in translation and I'm not fully understanding what it's the intended writers design.<br /> <br /> I thought the moon effect where linked to the quantity of the moon showed into the sky (as for the Auspices) and so linked to Crescent/Gibbous and not to Waxing Waning. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_relative text_table_table-fixed\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>Moon Phase</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>Rage gain (CANON)</b></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>What I think is more reasonable</b></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf11 New</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf12 Waxing Crescent</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3 (?)</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>+2</b></b> \u2190 changed</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf13 First Quarter / Half</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf14 Waxing Gibbous</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf15 Full</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+4</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf16 Waning Gibbous</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+2 (?)</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\"><b><b>+3</b></b> \u2190 changed</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf17 Last Quarter / Half</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3 (?)</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf18 Waning Crescent</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_relative_tr text_table_table-fixed_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">\ud83c\udf11 New</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_px-sm text_table_py-xs text_table_leading-5 text_table_border text_table_border-solid text_table_border-neutral-border text_table_relative_td text_table_table-fixed_td\">+1</td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T13:49:52-07:00","id":1553431,"title":"","content":"You're reading the text correctly. Though your proposed house rule is extremely common (so common a lot of people don't even realize it is one because they've always played it that way).<br /> <br /> Another potential change is just: 1/3/3/3/4/2/<b>2</b>/2/1. It doesn't have the same gradual flow with the changing of the moon, but it keeps to the waxing/waning separation (something that is otherwise absent from the rules even though the Garou supposedly put value in it as well as the specific moon phases).<br /> <br /> Ultimately it really doesn't matter that much in play unless you're in a game that moves at a very slow pace in-universe (that is, most sessions only cover ~1-2 days of events, and there is very little downtime between events, so a month of weekly gaming might only cover a week's worth of in-universe time). When you're just playing and the ST largely picks the time of the month to spread around the effects on the PCs and there's more time passing between played events, the impact of this is much harder to really feel in-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T15:45:55-07:00","id":1553433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553415-w20-new-st-help-with-rage-gain-and-moon-phases?p=1553431#post1553431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're reading the text correctly. Though your proposed house rule is extremely common (so common a lot of people don't even realize it is one because they've always played it that way).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost a week I'm talking with players on the subject and a lot of them noticed it now for the first time! They didn't knew they always played an house rule (mine o the equally valid 1/3/3/3/4/2/<b>2</b>/2/1 you proposed).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T19:16:06-07:00","id":1553436,"title":"","content":"I've been using 1/2/3/3/4/3/3/2/1 for probably 20 years as my default house rule (the 1/3/3/3/4/2/2/2/1 I do like better in theory but most people like the other one more IME). I was just aware of it and part of discussions on running it differently. Hell, it's possible I was part of a group that helped normalize it so much:<br /> <br /> Back in the final years of the original run of the WoD, there was a persistent online chat based game on the White Wolf website called New Bremen. It used the method you proposed, and while I wasn't part of that decision, some of the people that were did participate in the debate on this on the old WoD BBS that was going on shortly before. And I will say that it definitely works better for something like that sort of chat. If you're not familiar, the game is basically always &quot;open&quot; for players to run around, rather than people only coming together to play at set times like traditional TTRPG sessions. This meant things like what time of day it was in-character, what the current moon-phase, and so on had to be partially automated so players could resolve things like &quot;what's the Frenzy difficulty for Garou?&quot; even if no STs were present.<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of the New Bremen house rules that were put in place because of the change in format crop up in the intervening decades in the &quot;didn't even realize that was a house rule,&quot; category. Which can't be that surprising as it had a lot of players and a decent international player base for the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T22:07:56-07:00","id":1553455,"title":"","content":"Excellent comments all around. If I was going to use a logical system that tried to account for the &quot;waxing moon is stronger Rage, and waning moon is weaker Rage&quot;, it would be 1/2/3/3/4/3/2/2/1. The progression makes sense, but it adjusts the half moon &quot;appropriately&quot; to reflect whether it is waxing or waning. If you don't want to showcase waxing as stronger Rage, the other variants are equally good. (1/2/3/3/4/3/3/2/1 is at least consistent and intuitive.)<br /> <br /> My opinion is that in some cases, the writers of the sourcebooks did not bother to think things through all the time. What they wrote is not always what they intended. They probably meant &quot;gibbous moon&quot; instead of &quot;waxing moon&quot;, and &quot;crescent moon&quot; instead of &quot;waning moon&quot;. But they wrote what they wrote. Strange anomalies therefore show up. <br /> <br /> You have to house rule some things to get more practical rules. The new versions of the corebooks were often just copied verbatim the earlier edition instead of being properly updated with errata and the like. The pattern you noted is something that should have been corrected long ago.<br /> <br /> Use what you think best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}